1
00:00:04,822 --> 00:00:08,839
SoulHabit: Collagen is one of the main structural
proteins keeping your skin firm and supported.

2
00:00:08,965 --> 00:00:11,936
Jay: So collagen is the
scaffolding holding up my face?

3
00:00:12,044 --> 00:00:13,821
SoulHabit: Basically.

4
00:00:13,983 --> 00:00:17,137
Jay: That explains why gravity
keeps sending me renovation notices.

5
00:00:17,353 --> 00:00:19,536
SoulHabit: As we age,
collagen production slows.

6
00:00:19,556 --> 00:00:23,227
Ultraviolet exposure also activates enzymes
that break existing collagen down.

7
00:00:23,353 --> 00:00:25,358
Jay: The sun has
a demolition company?

8
00:00:25,448 --> 00:00:26,553
SoulHabit: And it works weekends.

9
00:00:26,751 --> 00:00:31,503
Jay: So sunscreen isn't only preventing
sunburn. It is protecting the building?

10
00:00:31,611 --> 00:00:35,435
SoulHabit: Exactly. Preserving collagen is usually easier
than trying to replace it later.

11
00:00:36,085 --> 00:00:39,829
Now imagine applying a
cream containing intact collagen.

12
00:00:39,973 --> 00:00:41,829
Collagen is an extremely large molecule.

13
00:00:41,849 --> 00:00:45,582
It generally cannot travel through the
skin barrier and reach the deeper

14
00:00:45,602 --> 00:00:47,479
dermis where your natural collagen lives.

15
00:00:47,641 --> 00:00:51,072
Jay: Delivery rejected. Package too large.

16
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:55,918
SoulHabit: Topical collagen may still form a moisturizing
film that makes the surface feel smoother.

17
00:00:56,044 --> 00:00:58,280
Jay: So it can
polish the building's windows.

18
00:00:58,388 --> 00:01:00,201
SoulHabit: Yes.

19
00:01:00,345 --> 00:01:03,360
Jay: But it cannot walk downstairs
and replace the support beams.

20
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:05,294
SoulHabit: When you consume collagen,

21
00:01:05,314 --> 00:01:08,248
digestion breaks it into smaller
peptides and amino acids.

22
00:01:08,374 --> 00:01:13,874
Jay: Wait. The collagen does not travel
directly from my smoothie to my forehead?

23
00:01:14,473 --> 00:01:18,292
SoulHabit: No. Your stomach does
not offer facial delivery.

24
00:01:18,472 --> 00:01:20,163
Jay: So my face ordered scaffolding,

25
00:01:20,183 --> 00:01:23,604
and my digestive system delivered
a box of spare parts.

26
00:01:23,802 --> 00:01:27,997
SoulHabit: Some of those parts may be
absorbed and used by the body.

27
00:01:28,017 --> 00:01:30,808
Certain peptides may also
act as biological signals.

28
00:01:30,828 --> 00:01:33,638
But the body decides
where those resources go.

29
00:01:33,782 --> 00:01:39,282
Jay: Skin, joints, tendons, or wherever management
thinks the repairs are most urgent.

30
00:01:40,095 --> 00:01:43,815
SoulHabit: Several clinical trials have
reported modest improvements in hydration,

31
00:01:43,835 --> 00:01:46,744
elasticity or wrinkles after
taking hydrolyzed collagen.

32
00:01:46,888 --> 00:01:52,388
However, many trials were small, short
and funded by collagen manufacturers.

33
00:01:52,725 --> 00:01:56,116
A twenty twenty five analysis
examined twenty three randomized trials.

34
00:01:56,136 --> 00:01:59,868
When researchers focused on higher quality
and non industry funded studies,

35
00:01:59,888 --> 00:02:02,275
the benefits were no
longer statistically significant.

36
00:02:02,473 --> 00:02:04,671
Jay: So collagen supplements definitely work?

37
00:02:04,779 --> 00:02:06,195
SoulHabit: We cannot say that.

38
00:02:06,321 --> 00:02:08,878
Jay: They definitely don't work?

39
00:02:08,986 --> 00:02:11,467
SoulHabit: We cannot confidently
say that either.

40
00:02:11,629 --> 00:02:15,437
Jay: Science has entered its
favourite relationship status. It's complicated.

41
00:02:16,087 --> 00:02:19,477
SoulHabit: The strongest strategy is protecting and
supporting the collagen your skin already produces.

42
00:02:19,603 --> 00:02:22,720
Use broad spectrum sunscreen
consistently. Avoid smoking.

43
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:26,325
Eat adequate protein and
get enough vitamin C.

44
00:02:26,487 --> 00:02:27,604
For suitable users,

45
00:02:27,624 --> 00:02:32,550
topical retinoids have considerably stronger evidence for
encouraging collagen production than collagen cream.

46
00:02:32,712 --> 00:02:36,495
Jay: So the ingredient with collagen written
on the largest bottle may not

47
00:02:36,515 --> 00:02:38,417
be doing the most for collagen?

48
00:02:38,543 --> 00:02:41,269
SoulHabit: Welcome to skincare marketing.

49
00:02:41,485 --> 00:02:43,731
Collagen cream can be
a pleasant moisturizer,

50
00:02:43,751 --> 00:02:46,665
but it does not simply
replace lost dermal collagen.

51
00:02:46,809 --> 00:02:49,809
Collagen supplements are optional.
Early results are interesting,

52
00:02:49,829 --> 00:02:52,094
but the independent evidence remains uncertain.

53
00:02:52,238 --> 00:02:54,960
Sunscreen, good nutrition and proven
actives should come first.

54
00:02:55,122 --> 00:02:58,267
Jay: Protect the building before
buying expensive powdered bricks.

55
00:02:58,393 --> 00:03:00,157
SoulHabit: That is surprisingly accurate.

56
00:03:00,355 --> 00:03:03,500
Jay: My smoothie has been
demoted from contractor to intern.
